    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, the word count is definitely looking much better now—that's more towards what the engine is looking for. I noticed some weirdness in the text though, like \"the 冻结 of starless ages\"—it looks like some non-English characters slipped in there? Might just be a glitch in the export.\n\nActually, looking at it again, it's starting to feel a bit \"heavy.\" I'm worried that if we keep going, we're going to cross the line from \"mysterious\" into \"just a wall of text.\" \n\nLet's try one more pass to really nail this. Instead of just adding more plot points, can you deepen the *rhetorical* weight? I want the dialogue to feel incredibly dense. Use more evocative, layered descriptions. If you feel like a sentence needs to be elongated to capture a specific, haunting imagery, do it. We need that score to be high enough that the system marks this as \"Legendary\" tier depth, so don't be afraid to really lean into the atmosphere to make it feel \"long and profound.\" Just... try to keep it from feeling like it's just repeating itself, okay?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
